 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Cleaning your brushes keeps them working at their best. Plastic brushes can be washed with water, while oil based paints need a special cleaner. That's not ideal. Water corrodes the brush, making it stiffer. Sometimes, with lot of back and forth, they recover. If not, they're worth replacing. Then buy fresh ones with your project in mind. Good quality brushes last years.",
